  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The entropy versus temperature plot for phases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> bar pressure is given. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are entropies of the phases at temperatures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, respectively.</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/0e77b90b-182d-480f-bdcd-05844a779e2a.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 203px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>The transition temperature for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> phase change is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Assume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is independent of temperature in the range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></mrow></msub></math> are heat capacities of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> phases, respectively.</p>\n<br>The value of enthalpy change, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math> (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Jmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> ), at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "300",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>According to Kirchhoff&#39;s law&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><mn>600</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><mn>300</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mn>600</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now, at transition temperature,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><mn>600</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T&#916;S</mi><mn>600</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>600</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><mn>300</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>300</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><mn>300</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>600</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>300</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p></blockquote>",
